    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11607" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">crīmĭno</span></b> , āre,
			1, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>v.
				a.;</i> collat. form of criminor, <i>to accuse,
				make an accusation</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">aliquem apud aliquem,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps. 1, 5, 78</span></i>
			.— <b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: apud aliquem, Enn. ap. <i><span class="en">Non. p. 470,
				16</span></i> (Sat. v. 9 Vahl.).—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<i>Pass.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Sullanas res defendere criminor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Agr. 3, 4, 13</span></i>
			 dub. Orell. <i>N. cr.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">criminatum esse ab aliquo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hyg. Astr. 2, 18</span></i>
			.</div>
